        "orario": "17:48",
        "timestamp": 1776700083,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. 'Hierarchy of sovereignty': Israel claims authority over 'which Lebanese areas are inhabitable' Middle East Issued on: 20/04/2026 - 17:48 Modified: 20/04/2026 - 17:58 Carys Garland is pleased to welcome Nadim Houry, Executive Director of the Arab Reform Initiative (ARI). According to Houry, the “Yellow Line doctrine” is not a security measure, but rather a military tool for territorial control. Drawing on recent developments in Gaza, Syria, and Lebanon, he argues that this doctrine operates as a legal façade for expanding occupation under the language of self-defence. All the while, these practices actually undermine both ceasefire agreements and established principles of international law, threatening Lebanon's sovereignty. US seizes Iranian-flagged cargo ship 20/04/2026 Middle East 'US military leverage a risky tactic': Bombs, military escalation will not bring Iran 'to the table' 20/04/2026 Middle East Trump sending US delegation for Iran talks in Pakistan 19/04/2026 Middle East 'Ceasefire in the Middle East, especially in Lebanon, are meant to be broken', analyst says 19/04/2026 Middle East Iran asserts leverage in Hormuz ahead of new round of talks 19/04/2026 Middle East Israel's double game between negotiations with Lebanon and occupation in the south 19/04/2026 Middle East Food security under threat as Middle East war disrupts fertiliser supply 19/04/2026 Middle East A petition called 'Lebanon will not be the next Gaza' calls on French leaders to take action 19/04/2026 Middle East Iran: Prolonged conflict reshapes view of the regime, analyst says 19/04/2026 Middle East"
